title: Assembly Elections
new-page: true
tags: event
priority: -2
view-if: (year = next_election_year and month >= next_election_month and (next_election_week == week or not rubicon)) or (year > next_election_year)
on-arrival: election_boycott = 0
on-departure: in_election = 0; next_election_year = next_election_year + 4; n_elections += 1; next_election_time = time + 48
set-jump: post_election_1928
set-bg: img/map_2.jpg
#face-image: img/Rothe_Wahlen_1903.jpg


= Elections, [+ month : month +] [+ year_display +]

The Assembly elections are to be held now.

- @election_algorithm: May we do our best...
- @cancel_elections
- @boycott_elections

@cancel_elections
title: We cannot hold the elections now. Cancel the elections.
subtitle: This is an anti-democratic move that may backfire.
view-if: in_emergency_government == 1 and president_ideology == "Left" and not presidential_powers

Since we are currently ruling as part of an emergency government, we may use quasi-constitutional trickery to significantly delay these elections, and continue governing via the Emergency Articles. This is likely to be extremely unpopular both with our base and with the other parties. However, this may be necessary to prevent the extremists from gaining power.

- @cancel_elections_2: Yes, do it.
- @election_algorithm: No, let's hold the elections.

@cancel_elections_2
on-departure: next_election_year = next_election_year + 1; next_election_time = time + 12; pro_republic -= 10; gold_relation -= 8; lvp_relation -= 8; unionist_relation -= 8; ddp_relation -= 10; collectivist_relation -= 8; coup_progress += 2; commons_marcher -= 4; burgher_marcher -= 5; guild_marcher -= 5; landed_marcher -= 5; faithful_marcher -= 5; disfavored_marcher -= 5; coup_progress += 2 if royalist_normalized >= 0.3; coup_progress += 2 if royalist_normalized + traditionalist_normalized >= 0.5 and traditionalist_ideology = "Radical"; coup_progress += 2 if royalist_normalized + dnf_normalized >= 0.5 and traditionalist_ideology = "Moderate"; loyalist_strength += 100 if coup_progress >= 7; warden_strength += 100 if coup_progress >= 7
achievement: ausnahmezustand

Fine. President [+ president +] has taken the unprecedented step of canceling these elections. New elections are scheduled for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year + 2365 +].

Let us hope this does not backfire.

@boycott_elections
title: Boycott the elections. Staal will rig it anyway.
subtitle: Maybe the other parties will join us.
view-if: chancellor == "Staal" and staal_post and gnu_total_votes >= 30

There’s little point in participating in an election that’s clearly rigged. The most we can do is boycott the vote—depress turnout and deny Staal the legitimacy he desperately needs. But if we aren’t strong enough, we’ll simply hand the <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">**GNU**</span> a majority government on a silver platter.

However, if we commit, we might bring the other anti-Staal parties into the boycott as well. Strength in numbers.

Are we sure?

- @boycott_elections_2: Yes, do it.
- @election_algorithm: No, let's participate in the elections.

@boycott_elections_2
on-arrival: boycott_count = 0;
go-to: boycott_elections_menu

Alright. We'll see whether the other parties share the same sentiment. We already know the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>[? if sapd_formed:&nbsp;and <span style="color: #9B0000;">**Laborists**</span>?] are with us—who else?

@boycott_elections_menu

- @spd_boycott
- @center_boycott
- @liberals_boycott
- @right_boycott
- @nazis_boycott
- @boycott_elections_3

@spd_boycott
title: Check in our own party.
subtitle: The workers may have a different mindset.
on-arrival: {!
Q.boycott_count += 1;
Q.marcher_boycott_efficacy = 1;

if (Q.dissent) Q.marcher_boycott_efficacy -= Q.dissent;
if (Q.unions_independent) Q.marcher_boycott_efficacy -= 0.4;
if (!Q.unions_independent && Q.labor_dissent) Q.marcher_boycott_efficacy -= (Q.labor_dissent / 150);
if (Q.pro_republic >= 30) Q.marcher_boycott_efficacy += (Q.pro_republic / 150);
if (Q.marcher_boycott_efficacy > 1) Q.marcher_boycott_efficacy = 1;
!}
view-if: boycott_count < 5
max-visits: 1
go-to: boycott_elections_menu

The efficacy of our boycott depends on two key factors: party dissent and our control over labor. If the Staal-sympathetic factions within the Free Guilds and the party choose to vote for the <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">**GNU**</span> regardless, our boycott will be in vain.

Boycott efficacy: [+ marcher_boycott_efficacy : boycott_efficacy +]

@center_boycott
title: Check in the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>.
subtitle: [? if not unionist_gnu: Relations: [+ unionist_relation : relationships +] ?][? if unionist_gnu: <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> - Bloc Party Status?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.boycott_count += 1;
Q.unionist_boycott_efficacy = 1;

Q.unionist_boycott_efficacy -= ((100 - Q.unionist_relation) / 200);
if (!Q.united_labor) Q.unionist_boycott_efficacy -= 0.2;
Q.unionist_boycott_efficacy -= ((100 - Q.pro_republic) / 250);
if (Q.unionist_leader == "Sedgewick") Q.unionist_boycott_efficacy += 0.1;
if (!Q.unionist_in_gov) Q.unionist_boycott_efficacy += 0.2;
if (Q.unionist_gnu || Q.unionist_boycott_efficacy < 0.2) Q.unionist_boycott_efficacy = 0.2;
if (Q.unionist_boycott_efficacy > 1) Q.unionist_boycott_efficacy = 1;
!}
view-if: boycott_count < 5
max-visits: 1
go-to: boycott_elections_menu

[? if not unionist_gnu: The <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> is internally split on this. Their ties to the Staal cabinet and the pro-Staal sentiment expressed by many of their party members have made joining the <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span>-led boycott a hard pill to swallow. However, we have gained the sympathy of their left wing. ?][? if unionist_gnu: The <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> is already a <i>bloc party</i>, so it's out of the question. However, we have some sympathetic voices on the party's left wing, like Werth and Aldwin Stilling of the <span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span> Free Guilds, lending their support nonetheless. ?]

Boycott efficacy: [+ unionist_boycott_efficacy : boycott_efficacy +]

@liberals_boycott
title: Check in the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberals</span>.
subtitle: [? if lvp_formed and not lvp_gnu: Relations: [+ lvp_relation : relationships +] ?][? if lvp_formed and lvp_gnu: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> - Bloc Party Status?][? if not lvp_formed and not gold_exist and not dstp_gnu: Relations: [+ ddp_relation : relationships +] ?][? if not lvp_formed and not gold_exist and dstp_gnu: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> - Bloc Party Status ?][? if not lvp_formed and gold_exist: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> [? if not dstp_gnu: relations: [+ ddp_relation : relationships +] ?][? if dstp_gnu: - Bloc Party Status ?] <br> <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> [? if not gold_gnu: relations: [+ gold_relation : relationships +] ?][? if gold_gnu: - Bloc Party Status ?] ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.boycott_count += 1;
Q.lib_boycott_efficacy = 1;
if (Q.dstp_gnu) Q.lib_boycott_efficacy -= 0.4;
if (Q.gold_gnu) Q.lib_boycott_efficacy -= 0.4;
if (Q.lvp_gnu) Q.lib_boycott_efficacy -= 0.8;

if (!Q.lvp_formed) Q.lib_boycott_efficacy -= ((100 - Q.ddp_relation) / 400);
if (Q.ddp_leader != "Lindell" && !Q.lvp_formed) Q.lib_boycott_efficacy += 0.2;
if (Q.lvp_formed) Q.lib_boycott_efficacy -= ((100 - Q.lvp_relation) / 400);
if (!Q.lvp_formed && Q.gold_relation >= 40) Q.lib_boycott_efficacy += (Q.gold_relation / 400);
if (Q.ddp_ideology == "Right" && !Q.lvp_formed) Q.lib_boycott_efficacy -= 0.1;
if (Q.gold_ideology != "Right" && !Q.lvp_formed) Q.lib_boycott_efficacy += 0.1;
if (Q.lvp_formed && Q.lvp_ideology == "Left") Q.lib_boycott_efficacy += 0.2;
if (Q.united_labor && !Q.lvp_formed) Q.lib_boycott_efficacy += 0.2;
if (Q.united_labor && Q.lvp_formed) Q.lib_boycott_efficacy += 0.1;
Q.lib_boycott_efficacy -= ((100 - Q.pro_republic) / 250);
if (Q.rdp_list) Q.lib_boycott_efficacy += 0.1;
if (!Q.unionist_in_gov) Q.lib_boycott_efficacy += 0.1;
if (Q.lib_boycott_efficacy < 0.4 || (Q.gold_gnu || Q.dstp_gnu)) Q.lib_boycott_efficacy = 0.4;
if (Q.lib_boycott_efficacy < 0.2 || (Q.gold_gnu && Q.dstp_gnu || Q.lvp_gnu)) Q.lib_boycott_efficacy = 0.2;
if (Q.lib_boycott_efficacy > 1) Q.lib_boycott_efficacy = 1;
!}
view-if: boycott_count < 5
max-visits: 1
go-to: boycott_elections_menu

[? if not lvp_gnu and lvp_formed: As much as we expect the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> to put up a defense of the Republic, since they're liberal, pro-Staal elements run rampant throughout the party. We can, however, expect strong support from their left wing and intelligentsia. ?][? if lvp_gnu and lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> have succumb to Staal's influence, becoming a <i>bloc party</i>. We can only expect support from the miniscule <span style="color: #E0B0FF;">**RDP**</span>. ?]

[? if not lvp_formed and not dstp_gnu: The <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> are effectively dead electorally and offer little of value to us. However, they are embroiled in an internal struggle, and surprisingly, the business wing of the party—figures like Hewes and Dietrich—are more inclined to align with us than the left wing's Lindell. ?][? if not lvp_formed and dstp_gnu: The <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> have fully fallen under Staal's influence. Not like their electorally dead party could offer much impact anyway. ?]

[? if not lvp_formed and gold_exist and not gold_gnu: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> is quite distant from us, even more so as they drift under Staal's influence. [? if gold_relation < 40: We cannot expect them to take part in a <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span>-led boycott. ?][? if gold_relation >= 40: We can count on the support of Strattonites like Holt and Curthose to lobby the party. ?] ?][? if not lvp_formed and gold_exist and gold_gnu: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> is firmly under Staal's control, and their leadership is far too hostile to us to consider participation, even if they weren’t a <i>bloc party</i>. ?]

Boycott efficacy: [+ lib_boycott_efficacy : boycott_efficacy +]

@right_boycott
title: Mallin can be relied on.
subtitle: We can count on him to boycott the elections.
on-arrival: {!
Q.boycott_count += 1;
!}
view-if: boycott_count < 5
max-visits: 1
go-to: boycott_elections_menu

On the right, we can only truly count on Mallin and what remains of his followers to boycott the election, as he remains a mortal enemy of the chancellor. However, his stance of total opposition is deeply unpopular—even among his most fanatically loyal supporters, many of whom are likely to vote for Staal anyway.

@nazis_boycott
title: Perhaps the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> could participate..?
subtitle: We shouldn't expect much.
on-arrival: {!
Q.boycott_count += 1;
!}
view-if: boycott_count < 5
max-visits: 1
go-to: boycott_elections_menu

It appears that the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> and <span style="color: #6A1E1E;">**CSG**</span> haven’t abandoned their ballot-box tactics and have chosen to participate in the elections regardless. [? if nvf_exist and not nvf_gnu: The <span style="color: #142e20;">**NPF**</span>, however, have boycotted, preferring to pool their limited resources into the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> rather than waste them on a costly electoral campaign. ?]

@boycott_elections_3
title: We have finished negotiations.
on-arrival: {!
Q.election_boycott = 1;
!}
view-if: boycott_count >= 5

Hopefully, this will have some effect.

- @election_algorithm: We've done enough.

