unavailable-subtitle: <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">GNU</span> + <span style="color: #c00000;">Marchers</span>[? if not unionist_gnu:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #000000;">[+ unionist_party_name +]</span> + <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">Arcanists</span>?][? if not lvp_formed and not dstp_gnu:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #D3C24D;">[+ ddp_name +]</span>?][? if lvp_formed and not lvp_gnu:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span>?] ([+ staal_left_coalition +]%) [? if rubicon: - President DuFour will never permit Staal to bring <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformists</span> into the government, no matter his ulterior motive. ?]
choose-if: president != "DuFour"
on-arrival: leverage -= 10; leverage += 5; leverage += 5 if unionist_ideology == "Left"; in_staal_left_coalition = 1; marcher_in_government = 1; vice_chancellor = "Sedgewick"; heartland_leader = "Goodlake" if heartland_leader == "Staal" or heartland_leader == "Crowde"; foreign_minister_party = "GNU"; interior_minister_party = "GNU"; justice_minister_party = "Unionist"; justice_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; labor_minister_party = "Unionist"; army_minister_party = "GNU"; economic_minister_party = "GNU"; finance_minister_party = "GNU"; agriculture_minister_party = "GNU"; labor_minister = "Sedgewick"; army_minister = "Staal"; pro_republic += 5; staal_marcher_influence += 4; dufour_angry = -500; staal_approval += 2

Staal has his parliamentary cabinet, and the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> have a seat at the table. Whether the general means to share power, or merely to borrow it, remains to be seen.

