Surprisingly, the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] agrees to a reform of the ruling Unity Coalition. The Minister-President position is transferred from Bristol to[? if left_split == 1:&nbsp;<span style="color: #9B0000;">**Laborists**</span> member?] Cael Pendrigon, who [? if left_split == 0: belongs?][? if left_split == 1: belonged?] to the left faction of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, and had a history of defending <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> members through his work. He is accepted with great reluctance to the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and welcomed by the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.

The right will be more active in resisting our rule considering we are going to rule with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> on both levels of government. The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> has provided a list of objectives for us to complete in parallel to our federal policies.

