We have kicked out the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> from the government, and formed a Popular Front. The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> is infuriated by our betrayal and any future coalitions with them may be impossible. The Minister-President position is transferred from Bristol to[? if left_split == 1:&nbsp;<span style="color: #9B0000;">**Laborists**</span> member?] Cael Pendrigon, who [? if left_split == 0: belongs?][? if left_split == 1: belonged?] to the left faction of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, and had a history of defending <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> members through his work. He is accepted with great reluctance to the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and welcomed by the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.

The right will be more active in resisting our rule considering we are going to rule with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> on both levels of government. The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> has provided a list of objectives for us to complete in parallel to our federal policies.

[? if president_ideology == "Right" or president == "DuFour": [+ president +] might object to this coalition, and may perform a <i>Commonwealth intervention</i> on our Heartland government, if we were to become too radical in our actions.?]

- @prussia_election_1928.kpd_goals_prussia: The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> presents us with a list of demands.

@great_popular_front
view-if: unionist_ideology == "Left" and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators"
on-arrival: marcher_in_government = 1; in_popular_front = 1; chancellor = "Yardley"; chancellor_party = "Marcher"; collectivist_relation += 10; coup_progress += 1; in_left_front = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; coalition_dissent = 0; coup_progress += 1 if in_popular_front_heartland; capital_strike_progress += 1 if in_popular_front_heartland; dufour_angry = 70
achievement: grosse_volksfront
go-to: popular_front_civil_war if coup_progress >= 10; popular_front_no_civil_war if coup_progress < 10

Somehow, the coalition is successfully formed! The conciliatory leadership of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> helped make the negotiations possible. We still need a chancellor; the only acceptable choice among the parties was Calbert Yardley of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, acceptable to the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> [? if president == "DuFour" or president_ideology == "Moderate": as well as President [+ president +], albeit extremely reluctantly ?].

@popular_front_success
on-arrival: marcher_in_government = 1; in_popular_front = 1; chancellor = "Yardley"; chancellor_party = "Marcher"; collectivist_relation += 10; coup_progress += 1; in_left_front = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; coalition_dissent = 0; coup_progress += 1 if in_popular_front_heartland; capital_strike_progress += 1 if in_popular_front_heartland; dufour_angry = 75
