unavailable-subtitle: Pendrigon would never allow this.
choose-if: president != "Pendrigon"
go-to: far_right_win if (year >= 1932 or royalist_r >= 44 or chancellor == "Goodlake") and president != "Bristol"; far_right_fail if (year < 1932 and royalist_r < 44 and chancellor != "Goodlake") and president != "Bristol"; far_right_braun if president == "Bristol"
priority: 2

There are enough votes for the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> and the [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> ?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span> ?] to form a coalition. [+ royalist_leader +] has made his participation in government contingent on being appointed chancellor. It is up to President [+ president +] to decide. As this is a parliamentary cabinet, [+ president +] is more likely to appoint [+ royalist_chancellor +].

@far_right_win
on-arrival: chancellor = royalist_chancellor; chancellor_party = "Royalist"

[? if president == "DuFour" : President DuFour's camarilla ?][? if president != "DuFour" and president != "Bristol": President [+ president +] ?][? if president == "Bristol" : President Bristol somehow ?] has decided that [+ royalist_leader +] must be chancellor [? if president == "DuFour": , and the aging president accepts their recommendations. ?][? if president != "DuFour" : because it is what the constitution would stipulate. ?]

- @hitler_takes_power: What do we do now?


@far_right_fail
face-image: img/portraits/goerdeler.jpg
on-arrival: {!
Q.chancellor = "Goodlake";
Q.chancellor_party = "I";
Q.gold_right += 3;
Q.lvp_right += 3;
Q.ddp_right += 1;
Q.ddp_cohesion -= 2;
Q.pro_republic -= 10;
