The <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> establishment is still very skeptical of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>, so instead, [+ president +] appoints Reynold Goodlake, the Mayor of Lindholt, as Chancellor, to try to "tame" the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>.

With [+ royalist_leader +] and Mallin refusing to join any reformed Askew cabinet, DuFour has sidestepped the issue by turning to the staunchly conservative Goodlake, who renounced his affiliation with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> to accept the post.

Upon taking office, however, Goodlake has yet to secure formal support from the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> or [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span>?]—support he needs, given that the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>[? if not lvp_formed:&nbsp;and likely the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?] will not back his government.

The coming months will reveal whether Goodlake can govern—and if the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> is truly serious about entering government.

@far_right_braun
on-arrival: coup_progress += 2

President [+ president +] faces a dilemma. Is it "democratic" to let democracy be destroyed, if the majority of voters have willed it so? Some, even on the left, suggest that the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> would not *truly* be as horrific as their platform suggests, and that giving them power would let them discredit themselves in the eyes of the public.

Alternatively, [+ president +] could use the emergency powers of the presidency. the Emergency Articles have been used by DuFour to promulgate anti-democratic and anti-worker policies; can the Emergency Articles be used for good as well as evil?

- @emergency_braun: We will form an emergency government with [+ president +]'s support.
- @new_elections: We will have new elections.
- @far_right_win: Let the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> form their government.


@left_coalition
title: Is a United Left coalition possible?
subtitle: <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> + <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> [? if sapd_formed: + <span style="color: #9B0000;">**Laborists**</span> ?] ([+ left_coalition +]%)
