There are enough votes for a <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> + <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> coalition government, if such a thing were actually possible.

The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> might attempt a coup, if such a coalition were formed.

- @left_coalition_impossible: This is impossible.
- @left_coalition_possible: This could be possible.

@left_coalition_impossible
go-to: coalition_menu

A far left coalition is impossible.


@left_coalition_possible

The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> is still very reluctant to join a coalition, despite grassroots friendliness between our memberships. The <span style="color: #8B0000;">hardline</span> leadership is vehemently against such a thing. They demand the appointment of Ernst Halsmark as chancellor in exchange for a coalition. [? if president_ideology != "Left" : There is no chance whatsoever that President [+ president +] would approve of the appointment of a die-hard collectivist as chancellor. ?] Alternatively, if our relations with them are good enough, we could convince them to support the appointment of one of our centrist or left-leaning members as chancellor.

- @thalmann_chancellor: Appoint Halsmark as chancellor.
- @left_coalition_resources
- @left_coalition_relations
- @coalition_menu: Try a different governing arrangement.

@thalmann_chancellor
choose-if: president_ideology == "Left" and reformist_strength + knight_strength < left_strength
unavailable-subtitle: [? if president_ideology != "Left": President [+ president +] would never allow such a thing. ?] [? if reformist_strength >= left_strength : Most in the parliamentary party would not support Halsmark as chancellor. ?]
on-arrival: chancellor = "Halsmark"; chancellor_party = "Collectivist"; collectivist_relation = 80; in_left_front = 1; marcher_in_government = 1 

With great reluctance, President [+ president +] appoints [+ chancellor +] as chancellor.

Immediately, [+ chancellor +] goes to work building a "<span style="color: #750e0e;">Collectivist Commonwealth</span>": consolidating as much power as possible in the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>, purging state institutions of anti-<span style="color: #700000;">collectivists</span>, and sending street fighters against the "enemies of the people".

In response to [+ chancellor +] being appointed Chancellor, the right-wing forces almost immediately launch an attempted coup. Troops of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> enter Axton and immediately begin clashing with our supporters! <span style="color: #808080;">Reactionary</span> officers within the Commonwealth Army have taken their troops out of the barracks and joined them with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> to stop the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> from taking power. We are forced to be on the same side as the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>, whether we want to or not.

- @civil_war


