Somehow, surprisingly, the left coalition is successfully formed, without appointing Halsmark as chancellor. The consensus choice for chancellor, accepted by the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>, and President [+ president +], is Calbert Yardley, who belongs to the centrist faction of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, but was acceptable to the left due to his previous membership in the left-wing anti-war <span style="color: #D47B9B;">**Independents**</span>.

# just raise the coup limit, don't immediately go to civil war

@left_coalition_no_civil_war
on-arrival: collectivist_goals_seen = 0; foreign_minister_party = "Marcher"; interior_minister_party = "Marcher"; justice_minister_party = "Marcher"; labor_minister_party = "Marcher"; army_minister_party = "Marcher"; economic_minister_party = "Marcher"; finance_minister_party = "Marcher"; agriculture_minister_party = "Marcher"; army_loyalty -= 0.05; gold_right += 10; ddp_right += 5; ddp_cohesion -= 3; lvp_right += 8; liberal_cooperation += 5; bourgeois_cooperation += 10; liberal_cooperation += 3 if in_left_front_heartland or in_popular_front_heartland; bourgeois_cooperation += 5 if in_left_front_heartland or in_popular_front_heartland; reformist_dissent += 20; reformist_strength -= 10; left_dissent -= 30; left_strength += 20; dufour_angry += 10 if in_popular_front_heartland or in_left_front_heartland; catastrophepolitik = 1 if n_elections >= 5 and not catastrophepolitik_cancel;
go-to: catastrophepolitik_left if catastrophepolitik = 1

In response to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>'s entrance into the government, the right-wing takes a "wait-and-see" approach for now. They expect that our government will be unstable and incompetent, and will collapse of its own accord, discrediting the left and eventually enabling the destruction of the Unity Republic. Our task is to prove them wrong. [? if in_left_front_heartland: The right will be more active in resisting our rule considering we are also ruling with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> in Heartland too. ?]

The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> has taken an abstentionist position with regards to ministries. They claim to be participating as the "loyal opposition" in the worker's government, supporting us from the outside while also running their own propaganda campaigns to turn workers to their side. They seem to expect that we would inevitably fail, and that our failure would benefit them. 

Whatever their reasoning is, the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> has control over the ministries of government.

@catastrophepolitik_left
achievement: catastrophepolitik

@left_coalition_civil_war
on-arrival: army_loyalty += 0.1

In response to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>'s entrance into the government, the right-wing immediately launches a coup attempt. Troops of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> enter Axton and begin clashing with our supporters. <span style="color: #808080;">Reactionary</span> officers within the Commonwealth Army have taken their troops out of the barracks and joined them with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> to stop us from taking power.

- @march_on_berlin_2: Fight against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Sovereigntists</span>!

@march_on_berlin_2
on-arrival: march_on_berlin_left = 1
go-to: march_on_berlin

@right_coalition
title: Refuse to form a government, so that a right-wing coalition may be formed.
subtitle: <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> + <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">**Arcanists**</span>[? if not lvp_formed and gold_exist:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed:&nbsp;+<span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] + **Others**[? if not concord_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?] ([+ right_coalition +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Traditionalists</span> is not interested in a coalition with the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?].
view-if: right_coalition >= 50 and not rubicon
choose-if: (traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" or traditionalist_westarp) and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7)
go-to: right_coalition_2 if grand_coalition < 50 or largest_party != "Marcher"

There are enough votes for a right-wing coalition of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] (+ <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">**Arcanists**</span>), [? if not lvp_formed and gold_exist: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?], <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, and minor conservative parties. [? if largest_party == "Marcher": However, this will be seen as abdicating responsibility for government, as we are the largest party. ?]

- @right_coalition_sure: Yes, we will abdicate our responsibility for government formation, and let a right-wing coalition take power.
- @grand_coalition: Actually, we wish to form a grand coalition after all.
- @weimar_coalition: Actually, we wish to form a Unity coalition after all.
- @weimar_coalition_liberal_parliament: Actually, we wish to form a Unity coalition after all.
- @popular_front_coalition: Actually, we wish to form a Popular Front coalition after all.


