The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] leader, [? if unionist_leader == "Hawkins": Cormac Hawkins?][? if unionist_leader == "Stilling": Aldwin Stilling?], clearly sees the threat from the ascension of the anti-democratic extremist parties, and thus tries to negotiate a "Government of National Unity" to save the republic. This coalition would be led by Joseph Werth, a left-leaning member of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and former chancellor, and would encompass all of the constitutional parties. Our role in this government might be limited, however.

- @unity_government_2
- @reject_unity_government: No, we will not accept this offer.

