There is, once again, no clear path to a majority government. Nevertheless, DuFour has reaffirmed his confidence in the chancellor and granted him permission to continue ruling by decree. With the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>'s poor electoral performance, the Camarilla is now convinced the party will be more reasonable in its demands and potentially open to tolerating the Goodryke cabinet.

Negotiations with [+ royalist_chancellor +] will resume in the coming weeks. However, Staal has begun to lose faith in Goodryke’s ability to reach an understanding with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>—and if these talks fail, it may be the final straw that turns the schemer against yet another of his old friends.

@no_majority_schleicher
on-arrival: dufour_staal_r -= 1; staal_strength -= 1; dufour_gallax_r += 1

Predictably, there is no clear path to a majority government, even with the fracturing of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>. DuFour is tired of the constant elections and presidential governments, but there is simply no way out. 

The prospect of negotiations with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> movement remains unobtainable, even with their electoral defeat causing even more defections and the shattering of their party morale. 

- @schleicher_dsu

@schleicher_dsu
title: Staal invites the <span style="color: #6A1E1E;">**CSG**</span> into cabinet?

Despite their addition barely doing much to grant Staal a majority, it signals a major step toward Staal's goal of integrating "favorable" <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> into the state—as he acknowledges that this is how much he's going to get. Their poor electoral performance will grant them few cabinet posts, but there remains substantial risks in letting the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> govern.

We could attempt to use our relations with the chancellor to prevent this, but he'll demand much concessions in return.

- @schleicher_dsu_yay
- @schleicher_dsu_nay

