Bram Frask is nominated to the Interior Ministry[? if old_heartland_leader == "Staal": in both the Commonwealth and Heartland, with the latter now under the control of [+ heartland_leader +], appointed as commissioner?]. Garrick Crowde takes the vice-chancellorship—a title without power.

At the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists’</span> insistence, Edrik Halbridge is named to the Economic Ministry as an independent. Varin Carlile, a <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> parliamentarian, receives the post of Minister without Portfolio.

Staal blocks <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> claims to the Labor Ministry, unwilling to provoke organized labor and still hoping to bring Adam Sedgewick—and the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>—into his coalition.

@schleicher_dsu_nay
title: Strike a deal with Staal.
subtitle: This is a point of no return.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if staal_marcher_r < 5: Our relations with Staal are too low. ?][? if staal_marcher_support < 8: Our party won't support compromising our independence. ?]
choose-if: staal_marcher_r >= 5 and staal_marcher_support >= 8

Exploiting our unusually good relations with the chancellor, we have moved to strike a deal with him to block <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> entry into the cabinet. We have threatened mass action by organized labor and the withdrawal of the Banners from his plans. Yet Staal sees greater advantage in aligning with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> regardless, and we are negotiating from a position of weakness.

What shall we give up?

- @schleicher_soul
- @schleicher_labor
- @schleicher_reichsbanner

@schleicher_soul
title: Staal strengthens his grip over the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> leadership.
subtitle: Our autonomy will be undermined.
on-arrival: staal_marcher_party = 1; staal_marcher_concession += 1; staal_marcher_influence += 4; dues -= 2 if dues > 1; commons_marcher -= 4; commons_collectivist += 2; burgher_marcher -= 4; burgher_collectivist += 4; left_dissent += 70; center_dissent += 50; reformist_strength += 20; labor_strength += 10; social_patriot_strength += 10; knight_strength -= 10; left_strength -= 20; center_strength -= 20; reformist_dissent += 20; knight_dissent += 40; labor_dissent += 40; nationalism += 20; pro_republic -= 10

Staal demands that his "supporters" be installed in leadership positions within the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, and that those already aligned with him, such as Bristol, be elevated further within the party hierarchy.

Furthermore, our commitments to pacifism, internationalism, and anti-militarism are being stripped out—not without backlash from our core interest groups.

- @schleicher_dsu_nay_2

@schleicher_labor
title: The Greater Worker's Guild falls under state influence.
subtitle: Class collaborationism will undermine the workers' power.
on-arrival: staal_marcher_labor = 1; staal_marcher_concession += 1; staal_marcher_influence += 3; commons_collectivist += commons_marcher*0.2; commons_marcher *= 0.8; disfavored_collectivist += disfavored_marcher*0.2; disfavored_marcher *= 0.8; dues -= 1 if dues > 1; labor_dissent += 40; labor_strength += 10; social_patriot_strength += 10; center_dissent += 40; left_dissent += 60; knight_dissent += 10; reformist_dissent += 10; pro_republic -= 10

We have convinced the Greater Worker's Guild to appoint some sketchy pro-Staal unionists to many top positions in the organization. Only time will tell what Staal will instruct his followers to do, but we can guess it has something to do with class solidarity for the goal of the Commonwealth's rearmament.

The working class is not entirely won over to the chancellor yet, and we stand to lose significant numbers of them to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.

- @schleicher_dsu_nay_2

@schleicher_reichsbanner
title: The Banners is integrated into the state.
subtitle: We will be defenseless.
on-arrival: staal_marcher_para = 1; staal_marcher_concession += 1; staal_marcher_influence += 2; army_strength += 75; army_militancy -= (1 - banner_militancy); banner_militancy = 0.02; banner_strength = 300; loyalist_strength += 50; vanguard_strength += 200; heartland_police_militancy = 1.5; heartland_police_strength += 15; commons_marcher -= 4; disfavored_marcher -= 6; burgher_marcher -= 2; commons_collectivist += 2; disfavored_collectivist += 4; knight_dissent += 60; knight_strength -= 10; labor_dissent += 30; center_dissent += 20; left_dissent += 50; reformist_dissent += 10; dues -= 1 if dues > 1; pro_republic -= 10

The Banners has been largely disarmed, with Staal promising increased funding for the police to maintain order in the streets.

The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> is demoralized, as many Banner members defect to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> and their <span style="color: #700000;">**Vanguard**</span>. We are now compelled to back the Commonwealth Army's auxiliaries in their campaigns against the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.

- @schleicher_dsu_nay_2

