Staal has suspended talks with the <span style="color: #6A1E1E;">**CSG**</span> by deliberately creating an impasse over control of the Interior Ministry. In the meantime, the absence of <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> in the cabinet has made it tolerable for the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> to return to government, with Adam Sedgewick securing the Labor Ministry and the nominal Vice Chancellorship, alongside other members claiming the Transport and Justice portfolios. The <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">**Arcanists**</span> is also granted the Postal Ministry. [? if unionist_leader == "Renck": Staal has also secured Aurelian Renck's backing by promising the immediate negotiation of a <i>Free Worship Accord</i>. ?]

[? if old_heartland_leader == "Staal": The Heartland <i>Commonwealth Commissioner</i> post is also handed from Staal to Goodlake—a signal that Staal has genuinely abandoned Goodryke's scheme for state centralization, and gestures toward an eventual return to democratic governance once stability is restored. Bristol is overjoyed at this, and argues that only a break with Staal would change his mind. ?]

The <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberals</span> and minor propertied parties have also rallied behind Staal once again. As part of our arrangement, he acknowledges the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>'s need to remain in opposition—a necessary measure, as a <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivist**</span> surge is an outcome neither of us desires.

