- @far_right_coalition



@emergency_braun
title: We will form an emergency government with [+ president +]'s support.
subtitle: This may have the effect of inflamming public sentiment against us, and the <span style="color: #808080;">reactionaries</span> will be against us each step of the way.
on-arrival: loyalist_strength += 100; warden_strength += 100; in_emergency_government = 1; ddp_relation -= 5; lvp_relation -= 5; gold_relation -= 5; unionist_relation -= 5; ddp_right += 1; ddp_cohesion -= 0.5; gold_right += 3; lvp_right += 1; bourgeois_cooperation += 5; liberal_cooperation += 3

Yes, an emergency minority government, with the support of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>. Who should lead this emergency minority government?

- @braun_emergency_chancellor: Lyle Bristol for Chancellor[? if president == "Bristol":-President?]!
- @breitscheid_emergency_chancellor: Calbert Yardley for emergency Chancellor.
- @bruning_emergency_chancellor: Askew of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], as a goodwill gesture toward the Burghers.
- @wirth_emergency_chancellor: Joseph Werth of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], as a gesture of <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> unity.

@braun_emergency_chancellor
subtitle: [? if president == "Bristol": This is unprecedented. ?][? if president != "Bristol": Perhaps more acceptable to the propertied parties... ?]
view-if: not historical_mode
on-arrival: chancellor = "Bristol"; chancellor_party = "Marcher"; marcher_in_government = 1; pro_republic -= 5; ddp_relation -= 4; gold_relation -= 4; unionist_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; gold_right += 2; ddp_right += 1.5; ddp_cohesion -= 1; lvp_right += 2; pro_republic += 3 if president != "Bristol"; ddp_relation += 4 if president != "Bristol"; gold_relation += 4 if president != "Bristol"; unionist_relation += 4 if president != "Bristol"; lvp_relation += 4 if president != "Bristol"; foreign_minister_party = "Marcher"; interior_minister_party = "Marcher"; justice_minister_party = "Marcher"; labor_minister_party = "Marcher"; army_minister_party = "Marcher"; economic_minister_party = "Marcher"; finance_minister_party = "Marcher"; agriculture_minister_party = "Marcher"; army_loyalty -= 0.1; bourgeois_cooperation += 3; liberal_cooperation += 3

[? if president == "Bristol": Our experts have checked the constitution, and have discovered that there is no specific prohibition against the Chancellor also being the President (the President may not be a member of the Assembly; there is no law saying that the Chancellor *must* be a member of the Assembly). ?][? if president != "Bristol": Lyle Bristol, one of our leading reformist politicians and statesmen, has been elevated to the second-highest office in the land. ?]

[? if president == "Bristol": Thus, we have Chancellor-President Lyle Bristol. He claims that he will resign as soon as the economic-political crisis is over. ?] The right-wing parties, who were once clamoring to replace parliamentary rule with <span style="color: #7A3C00;">dictatorship</span> or <span style="color: #808080;">monarchy</span>, are now clamoring for the restoration of democracy.

- @far_right_coup
- @emergency_no_confidence: The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> immediately call a no-confidence vote against us...

@breitscheid_emergency_chancellor
subtitle: The <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span> are warming to him...
on-arrival: chancellor = "Yardley"; chancellor_party = "Marcher"; marcher_in_government = 1; collectivist_relation += 5; ddp_relation -= 3; lvp_relation -= 3; gold_relation -= 3; unionist_relation -= 3; gold_right += 2; ddp_right += 1; ddp_cohesion -= 1; lvp_right += 1; foreign_minister_party = "Marcher"; interior_minister_party = "Marcher"; justice_minister_party = "Marcher"; labor_minister_party = "Marcher"; army_minister_party = "Marcher"; economic_minister_party = "Marcher"; finance_minister_party = "Marcher"; agriculture_minister_party = "Marcher"; army_loyalty -= 0.1;

We have appointed Calbert Yardley as emergency chancellor. The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> consider him less objectionable than the alternatives, although it is unclear whether they will tolerate this government.

- @far_right_coup
- @emergency_no_confidence


@bruning_emergency_chancellor
on-arrival: chancellor = "Askew"; chancellor_party = "Unionist"; marcher_in_government = 1; unionist_relation += 10; gold_relation += 3; ddp_relation += 3; lvp_relation += 3; foreign_minister_party = "Marcher"; interior_minister_party = "Marcher"; justice_minister_party = "Marcher"; labor_minister_party = "Marcher"; army_minister_party = "Marcher"; economic_minister_party = "Marcher"; finance_minister_party = "Marcher"; agriculture_minister_party = "Marcher" 

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is pleased, and somewhat surprised, that we have appointed [+ chancellor +] as chancellor.

- @far_right_coup
- @emergency_no_confidence

@wirth_emergency_chancellor
view-if: unionist_ideology == "Left"
on-arrival: chancellor = "Werth"; chancellor_party = "Unionist"; marcher_in_government = 1; unionist_relation += 10; gold_relation += 3; ddp_relation += 3; lvp_relation += 3; foreign_minister_party = "Marcher"; interior_minister_party = "Marcher"; justice_minister_party = "Marcher"; labor_minister_party = "Marcher"; army_minister_party = "Marcher"; economic_minister_party = "Marcher"; finance_minister_party = "Marcher"; agriculture_minister_party = "Marcher" 

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is pleased that we have appointed [+ chancellor +] as chancellor.

- @far_right_coup
- @emergency_no_confidence



@far_right_coup
title: The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> parties immediately launch a military coup against us...
view-if: far_right_coalition >= 45
on-arrival: warden_strength += 150; loyalist_strength += 150; warden_militancy += 0.05; loyalist_militancy += 0.05

The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> parties, seeing that we are willing to deny them government by questionably democratic means, have decided that they can only take power by undemocratic means, and have risen up in force against the sitting government.

Their numbers are bolstered by the many government workers who are against the prospect of a unified <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> government. Police and soldiers defect to the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span>.

- @civil_war: It is war.


@emergency_no_confidence
title: The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> immediately call a no-confidence vote against us...
view-if: far_right_coalition < 45
on-arrival: {!
Q.unionist_no_confidence = (Q.unionist_relation < 45) ? 1 : 0;
Q.collectivist_no_confidence = (Q.collectivist_relation < 45) ? 1 : 0;
Q.other_no_confidence = ((Q.unionist_relation + Q.gold_relation) / 2 < 45) ? 1 : 0;
Q.gold_no_confidence = (Q.gold_relation < 45) ? 1 : 0;
Q.ddp_no_confidence = (Q.ddp_relation < 35) ? 1 : 0;
Q.lvp_no_confidence = (Q.lvp_relation < 40) ? 1 : 0;

Q.loyalist_strength += 200;
Q.warden_strength += 200;

Q.no_confidence_votes = Q.royalist_r + Q.traditionalist_r + Q.dnf_r + Q.kvp_r;
Q.no_confidence_votes += (Q.unionist_no_confidence ? Q.unionist_r : 0);
Q.no_confidence_votes += (Q.gold_no_confidence ? Q.gold_r : 0);
Q.no_confidence_votes += (Q.ddp_no_confidence ? Q.ddp_r : 0);
Q.no_confidence_votes += (Q.lvp_no_confidence ? Q.lvp_r : 0);
Q.no_confidence_votes += (Q.collectivist_no_confidence ? Q.collectivist_r : 0);
Q.no_confidence_votes += (Q.other_no_confidence ? Q.other_r : 0);

Q.no_confidence_succeeds = (Q.no_confidence_votes > 50) ? 1 : 0;
Q.no_confidence_votes = parseFloat(Q.no_confidence_votes.toFixed(1));
!}

The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>[? if dnf_formed:, <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span>?][? if kvp_formed:, <span style="color: #0087DC;">**CPP**</span>?] and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> will vote against us, of course. The other parties vote their conscience. [? if unionist_no_confidence: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is voting against us. ?] [? if lvp_no_confidence and lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> will vote against us. ?] [? if collectivist_no_confidence: The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> votes against us. ?] [? if other_no_confidence: The assortment of minor parties are voting against us. ?]

In total, [+ no_confidence_votes +]% of the Assembly is against us. [? if no_confidence_succeeds : We have lost the vote of no confidence. ?]

- @no_confidence_elections_new: There will be new elections, which we will try to delay.
- @no_confidence_win: We have won, for now.


@no_confidence_elections_new
on-arrival: {!
Q.in_emergency_government = 1;
Q.no_majority_elections += 1;
Q.next_election_month = Q.month + 6;
Q.next_election_time = Q.time + 6;
if (Q.next_election_month > 12) {
    Q.next_election_month -= 12;
    Q.next_election_year = Q.year + 1;
} else {
    Q.next_election_year = Q.year;
}
Q.pro_republic -= 5;
Q.commons_marcher -= 3;
Q.burgher_marcher -= 3;
Q.guild_marcher -= 3;
Q.landed_marcher -= 3;
Q.faithful_marcher -= 3;
Q.commons_royalist += 5;
Q.guild_royalist += 3;
Q.burgher_royalist += 3;
Q.landed_royalist += 3;
Q.disfavored_royalist += 5;
// Thresholds are kind of arbitrary - adjusted because of negative economic effects on pro_republic
if (Q.pro_republic < 45 && Q.pro_republic >= 36) {
    Q.commons_marcher -= 6;
}
if (Q.pro_republic < 36) {
    // TODO: if you pursue a consistently revolutionary course, you might avoid this? But you might also cause a coalition between Gallax and the Center.
    Q.commons_marcher *= 0.85;
    Q.burgher_marcher -= 5;
    Q.guild_marcher -= 5;
    Q.landed_marcher -= 5;
    Q.faithful_marcher -= 3;
    Q.commons_royalist += 5;
    Q.guild_royalist += 5;
    Q.burgher_royalist += 5;
    Q.landed_royalist += 5;
    Q.disfavored_royalist += 5;   
}
!}
view-if: no_confidence_votes > 50

The next elections are set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year + 2365 +].


@no_confidence_win
view-if: no_confidence_votes <= 50
on-arrival: in_minority_government = 1; in_emergency_government = 0; catastrophepolitik = 1 if n_elections >= 5 and not catastrophepolitik_cancel;
achievement: minderheitsregierung
go-to: catastrophepolitik_minority if catastrophepolitik = 1

