We have enough votes to form a "<span style="color: #c00000;">Social</span>-[? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">Liberal</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">Liberal</span>?] Coalition" government consisting of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> and [? if ddp_name == "Gold" and not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**Democratic**</span>?][? if ddp_name == "CSP" and not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**State**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] [? if not lvp_formed: (<span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>)?][? if lvp_formed: (<span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>)?] party! This coalition has never been tested before and is only possible because the behemoth right-wing <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> includes certain <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> elements.

Who should be the chancellor?

@social_catholic_coalition_cvp
title: Can we form a <span style="color: #c00000;">Social</span>-<span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span> Coalition?
subtitle: <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> + <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> ([+ social_catholic_coalition +]%)
view-if: social_catholic_coalition >= 50 and concord_formed
unavailable-subtitle: <span style="color: #c00000;">Marchers</span> + <span style="color: #000000;">[+ unionist_party_name +]</span> ([+ social_catholic_coalition +]%) [? if not ((unionist_relation >= 70 and concord_ideology == "Moderate") or (unionist_relation >= 60 and concord_ideology == "Left")) and concord_ideology != "Right": - We do not have the adequate relations with the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Concord</span>?]. ?][? if concord_ideology == "Right": - Under its current leadership, the <span style="color: #000000;">[+ unionist_party_name +]</span> will never agree to a coalition with us. ?]
choose-if: ((unionist_relation >= 70 and concord_ideology == "Moderate") or (unionist_relation >= 60 and concord_ideology == "Left")) and concord_ideology != "Right"
go-to: social_catholic_coalition_cvp_negotiations

We have enough votes to form a "<span style="color: #c00000;">Social</span>-<span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span> Coalition" government consisting of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> and the <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>.  However, whether the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>—filled with <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalist</span> and staunchly anti-<span style="color: #9B0000;">Vaelist</span> elements—would ever truly accept such a coalition is another matter entirely. Still, the mere fact that they are even willing to engage in talks is an encouraging early sign.

@social_catholic_coalition_cvp_negotiations
on-arrival: {!

Q.concord_ministers_accepted = 0;
Q.concord_economy_accepted = 0;
Q.concord_chancellor_accepted = 0;
Q.concord_banner_accepted = 0;
Q.concord_women_accepted = 0;

Q.concord_negotiations_min = 50;

if (Q.unionist_votes >= Q.marcher_votes) {
    Q.concord_negotiations_min += (Q.unionist_votes - Q.marcher_votes)*2;
}

if (Q.concord_ideology == "Left") Q.concord_negotiations_min -= 10;
if (Q.unionist_relation >= 80) Q.concord_negotiations_min -= 10;
if (Q.royalist_votes >= 30) Q.concord_negotiations_min -= 10;
if (Q.pro_republic >= 75) Q.concord_negotiations_min -= 10;

if (Q.peoples_party) Q.concord_negotiations_min -= 5;
if (Q.left_split) Q.concord_negotiations_min -= 5;
if (Q.sapd_formed) Q.concord_negotiations_min -= 5;
if (Q.reformist_strength >= Q.left_strength + Q.center_strength) Q.concord_negotiations_min -= 5;

if (Q.nationalization_progress) Q.concord_negotiations_min += 15;
if (Q.economic_democracy) Q.concord_negotiations_min += 15;

if (Q.concord_negotiations_min > 55) {
    Q.concord_negotiations_min = 55;
}

Q.concord_negotiations_points = 0;
!}
go-to: cvp_demands_menu

We've met with the leadership of the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>, primarily those formerly from the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>, who have now presented their demands. There is some wiggle room regarding which demands we accept, and it’s up to us to use it wisely. Our previous actions also influence how lenient they are willing to be in pushing their demands.

The demands are listed in descending order of importance to the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>.

@cvp_demands_menu

- #cvp_demands
- @finalize_cvp_demands
- @refuse_cvp_demands
- #drop_cvp_demands

@cvp_ministers
title: Forfeit our rights to the Agriculture, Commonwealth Army, and Justice Ministry.
subtitle: This will bring an end to our efforts to reform the most backward and <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> parts of the Commonwealth.
tags: cvp_demands
view-if: concord_ministers_accepted = 0
on-arrival: concord_ministers_accepted = 1; concord_negotiations_points += 15
go-to: cvp_demands_menu

A demand put forth by their <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalist</span> wing, meeting this has secured us significant progress in negotiations.

@cvp_economy
title: Reject any form of socialization to the Commonwealth economy, and maintain a budgetary surplus at all times.
subtitle: This will limit our ability to reform the Commonwealth economy. [? if budget < 0: The state currently has a deficit, and austerity measures are required. ?]
tags: cvp_demands
view-if: concord_economy_accepted = 0
on-arrival: concord_economy_accepted = 1; concord_negotiations_points += 15;
go-to: cvp_demands_menu

A demand put forth by their <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalist</span> and <span style="color: #C0A054;">industrial</span> wing, meeting this has secured us significant progress in negotiations.

@cvp_chancellor
title: Forfeit our right to the Chancellorship.
subtitle: This will limit our ability to conduct government policy. [? if budget < 0 : We will be inheriting a deficit, so we will have to implement temporary austerity. ?]
tags: cvp_demands
view-if: concord_chancellor_accepted = 0
on-arrival: concord_chancellor_accepted = 1; concord_negotiations_points += 10;
go-to: cvp_demands_menu

A demand put forth by their <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalist</span> Right-<span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span>, and <span style="color: #C0A054;">industrial</span> wing, meeting this has secured us substantial progress in negotiations.

@cvp_reichsbanner
title: We must disarm the Banners.
subtitle: The <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> insist that they pose a threat to the stability of the government—and that the job should be left to the police.
tags: cvp_demands
view-if: concord_banner_accepted = 0
on-arrival: concord_banner_accepted = 1; concord_negotiations_points += 10;
go-to: cvp_demands_menu

A demand put forth by their <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalist</span> and right-<span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span> wing, meeting this has secured us substantial progress in negotiations.

@cvp_women
title: Abandon our efforts toward Women's and <span style="color: red;">Ho</span><span style="color: orange;">m</span><span style="color: yellow;">o</span><span style="color: green;">se</span><span style="color: blue;">xu</span><span style="color: purple;">al</span> rights.
subtitle: We will face backlash from advocacy groups.
tags: cvp_demands
view-if: concord_women_accepted = 0
on-arrival: concord_women_accepted = 1; concord_negotiations_points += 5;
go-to: cvp_demands_menu

A demand put forth by their <span style="color: #8ED8E4;">Faithful</span> wing, meeting this has secured us some progress in negotiations.

