We have enough votes to form a "Unity Coalition" government consisting of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and [? if ddp_name == "Gold" and not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**Democratic**</span>?][? if ddp_name == "CSP" and not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**State**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] [? if not lvp_formed: (<span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>)?][? if lvp_formed: (<span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>)?] parties. However the [? if liberal_parliament: liberals?][? if bourgeois_parliament_ddp: propertied?] are in a parliamentary group which prevents the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> from being included in our coalition by themselves.

We can either spend resources to convince the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> to break away from this arrangement, or to find another governing arrangement.

- @use_resources_weimar
- @coalition_menu: Try a different governing arrangement.

@use_resources_weimar
