The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] chancellor is likely to be Edmund Askew of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?][? if chancellor = "Askew" : &nbsp;again. ?][? if chancellor != "Askew": . ?] He is known for his conservatism and sympathy for monarchism, being on the right wing of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]. [? if austerity >= 2 : Due to the government's austerity policies, many of our members are reluctant to participate in this coalition again. Some support a "toleration" arrangement in which we will provide outside support to prevent the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> from either entering government or calling a successful no-confidence vote. Others support entering into pure opposition, and letting the right do what it wishes. ?]

Askew is not opposed to a coalition with us. Alternatively, we could enter a "toleration" agreement. [? if (right_coalition >= 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") or (center_right_coalition >= 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") : If we enter opposition, it is likely that Askew will enlist the support of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> [? if (right_coalition < 50 and center_right_coalition >= 50) and not lvp_formed: and the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]** </span> ?]to create a functioning majority. ?]

