Edmund Askew welcomes us into his new cabinet. Now, we have our pick of ministries. [? if in_grand_coalition_heartland and gold_heartland_asked = 0: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> are willing to grant us more cabinet posts as a result of including them in the Heartland cabinet. ?]

@bruning_oppo
on-arrival: marcher_in_government = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; chancellor = "Askew"; chancellor_party = "Unionist"; foreign_minister_party = "Gold"; foreign_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; interior_minister_party = "Unionist"; justice_minister_party = "Unionist"; labor_minister_party = "Unionist"; army_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = "Unionist"; finance_minister_party = "Unionist"; agriculture_minister_party = "Unionist"; grand_coalition_failed = 1

By refusing to join the grand coalition or tolerating it, we essentially throw the balance of government to the right wing. [? if right_coalition >= 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Radical" : There are enough votes to form a right-wing coalition that includes the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>. However, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> leader, Mallin, is opposed to a coalition with the "traitors of the Founding" of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]. And of course, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> is not interested in coalition government. This means that there will not be enough votes to form a majority coalition. ?][? if right_coalition >= 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" : There are enough votes to form a right-wing coalition that includes the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, and a collection of minor conservative parties. The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> is happy to join the government as to prevent the Askew cabinet from being dependent on our votes in a potential toleration agreement. ?][? if right_coalition < 50 and center_right_coalition >= 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" and not lvp_formed : There are not enough votes to form a right-wing coalition that includes the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, and a collection of minor conservative parties. However, this has been circumvented by the entrance of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> into the coalition. The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> is happy to join the government as to prevent the Askew cabinet from being dependent on our votes in a potential toleration agreement. ?][? if right_coalition < 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Radical" : There are not enough votes to form a right-wing coalition that includes the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, and they are not interested in joining in a coalition with the "traitors of the Founding" of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], anyhow. And of course, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> is not interested in coalition government. This means that there is no route to a majority coalition. ?][? if right_coalition < 50 and center_right_coalition < 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" and not lvp_formed : There are not enough votes to form a right-wing coalition that includes the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, and a collection of minor conservative parties, nor would there be enough votes if the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> participated too, Although, they both do enter Askew's presidential cabinet. And of course, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> is not interested in coalition government. This means that there is no route to a majority coalition. ?][? if right_coalition < 50 and center_right_coalition < 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" and lvp_formed: There are not enough votes to form a right-wing coalition that includes the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, and the collection of minor conservative parties. Although, they both do enter Askew's presidential cabinet. And of course, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> is not interested in coalition government. This means that there is no route to a majority coalition. ?]

[? if not (right_coalition < 50 and center_right_coalition >= 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" and not lvp_formed) or (right_coalition >= 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") : If we do not at least "tolerate" the government, there will be new elections in a few months. In the meantime, the President and Chancellor may use the emergency powers granted by the Unity Constitution to essentially govern by decree. And it is not at all clear that we will do any better in the next election. ?]

- @join_bruning: Join the Askew coalition[? if (right_coalition >= 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") or (center_right_coalition >= 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"): , to prevent a right coalition from forming?].
- @toleration_bruning: We will tolerate Askew after all.
- @toleration_bruning_right: We will tolerate Askew's right coalition government after all.
- @right_coalition_2: We will join the opposition.
- @center_right_coalition_2: We will join the opposition.
- @brauns_dilemma
- @new_elections: New elections, it is!


@new_elections
go-to: new_elections_2 if bruning_coalition >= 50 or year < 1930 or president != "DuFour" or rubicon_mini_leave; no_majority_goerdeler if bruning_coalition < 50 and year >= 1930 and president == "DuFour" and chancellor != "Goodlake" and not rubicon_mini_leave; no_majority_goerdeler_2 if bruning_coalition < 50 and year >= 1930 and president == "DuFour" and chancellor == "Goodlake" and not rubicon_mini_leave

@new_elections_2
on-arrival: {!
Q.next_election_month = Q.month + 3;
Q.next_election_time = Q.time + 3;
if (Q.next_election_month > 12) {
    Q.next_election_month -= 12;
    Q.next_election_year = Q.year + 1;
} else {
    Q.next_election_year = Q.year;
}
if (Q.chancellor == "Askew") {
    Q.unionist_relation -= 5;
    Q.gold_relation -= 5;
    Q.ddp_relation -= 5;
    Q.gold_right += 1;
    Q.ddp_right += 1;
    Q.lvp_relation -= 5;
    Q.lvp_right += 1;
}
Q.pro_republic -= 6;
Q.commons_marcher -= 4;
Q.burgher_marcher -= 4;
Q.guild_marcher -= 4;
Q.landed_marcher -= 4;
Q.faithful_marcher -= 2;
Q.burgher_gold -= 4;
Q.guild_gold -= 4;
Q.burgher_ddp -= 5;
Q.guild_ddp -= 5;
Q.burgher_lvp -= 4;
Q.guild_lvp -= 4;
Q.landed_traditionalist -= 5;
Q.commons_royalist += 5;
Q.guild_royalist += 6;
Q.burgher_royalist += 6;
Q.landed_royalist += 6;
Q.disfavored_royalist += 5;
if (Q.far_right_coalition >= 50) {
    Q.loyalist_strength += 100;
    Q.warden_strength += 100;
    Q.coup_progress += 3;
}
!}

There is no path to a workable Assembly majority or minority government. The next elections are set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year + 2365 +].

The people's faith in democracy is shaken by this ordeal. Of course, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> are exploiting the instability to claim that democracy is unworkable, and that the Commonwealth needs a strong leader.

@no_majority_goerdeler
on-arrival: {!
Q.chancellor = "Goodlake";
Q.chancellor_party = "I";
Q.gold_right += 3;
Q.lvp_right += 3;
Q.ddp_right += 1;
Q.ddp_cohesion -= 2;
Q.pro_republic -= 5;
!}
face-image: img/portraits/goerdeler.jpg

The prospect of new elections has proved daunting for the propertied parties—and for President DuFour himself. Disillusioned with Askew, DuFour and his Camarilla have cast him aside and appointed Reynold Goodlake, the Mayor of Lindholt, as Chancellor.

With [+ royalist_leader +] and Mallin refusing to join any reformed Askew cabinet, DuFour has sidestepped the issue by turning to the staunchly conservative Goodlake, who renounced his affiliation with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> to accept the post.

Upon taking office, however, Goodlake has yet to secure formal support from the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> or [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span>?]—support he needs, given that the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>[? if not lvp_formed:&nbsp;and likely the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?] will not back his government.

The coming months will reveal whether Goodlake can govern—and if the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> is truly serious about entering government.

@no_majority_goerdeler_2
on-arrival: {!
Q.chancellor = Q.royalist_chancellor;
Q.chancellor_party = "Royalist";

Q.rubicon_mini = 1;
Q.rubicon_mini_trigger = 1;
!}
