@new_elections_spd
on-arrival: next_election_time = time+3; next_election_month = month + 3; next_election_year = year; next_election_year = year + 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month = next_election_month - 12 if next_election_month > 12; burgher_marcher -= 5; guild_marcher -= 5; commons_marcher -= 3; faithful_marcher -= 3; in_election = 1

Since the remaining propertied and right-wing parties cannot form a tolerable governing agreement, new elections have been called for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year + 2365 +]. The previous chancellor has resigned, and has been replaced by Edmund Askew, also of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], ruling as part of a presidential cabinet. 

We are seen as responsible for the failure to form a government, and many of our middle-class and even some working-class supporters have deserted the party.


@ministries
on-arrival: {!
// The officer corps accepts a Marcher War Minister when the party's moderate wings
// outweigh its centrists and leftists (or one of those has walked out entirely) AND
// we have actually paid for the forces - funded an appropriation or voted through a
// war-galleon. Recomputed on every entry to the picker so it is never stale.
var _moderates = (Q.labor_strength || 0) + (Q.reformist_strength || 0) + (Q.knight_strength || 0);
var _radicals = (Q.center_strength || 0) + (Q.left_strength || 0);
var _dominant = (_moderates > _radicals) || Q.left_split || Q.centrists_resign;
Q.military_ministry_trusted = (_dominant && (Q.military_confidence || 0) >= 1) ? 1 : 0;
!}

We can pick from any number of ministries. Controlling a ministry allows us to directly effect policy in that area. [? if in_left_front : Any ministry that we do not take will be given to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>. ?] [? if in_left_front and army_minister_party == "Collectivist" : If the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> controls the Commonwealth Army Ministry, the army will most likely revolt. ?]

- @dvp_prussia_1: Offer the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> a spot in the Heartland government for more leverage.
- #mins_1928
- #drop_mins_1928

@labor
title: Labor Ministry
subtitle: Taking the Labor Ministry is expected of us.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1928
choose-if: leverage >= 5
view-if: labor_minister_party != "Marcher"
on-arrival: leverage -= 5; labor_minister_party = "Marcher"; labor_minister = "Wistle"
go-to: ministries

Rudolf Wistle of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> has been appointed labor minister.

