@dvp_prussia_1
subtitle: This will restrict our actions in Heartland.
view-if: year <= 1929 and in_grand_coalition_heartland = 0 and (in_weimar_coalition_heartland or in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland) and not in_left_front and not in_popular_front and not in_weimar_coalition and not in_emergency_government and gold_was_in_heartland == 0 and not lvp_formed and gold_exist
on-arrival: in_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 1; in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_popular_front_heartland = 0; in_left_front_heartland = 0; in_marcher_majority_heartland = 0; in_center_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_far_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; ddp_in_popular_front_heartland = 0; collectivist_goals_seen_heartland = 0; marcher_toleration_heartland = 0; leverage += 5; gold_relation += 7; unionist_relation -= 5; coalition_dissent = -1; left_dissent += 5; gold_left += 3; burgher_gold += 3
go-to: ministries

Letting the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> into the Heartland government is an offer too good for them to refuse, no matter their leadership. However, this will negatively impact our actions involving the Heartland police force due to the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> has ties to right-wing organizations such as the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Wardens</span>.

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] also is against this change because of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>'s opposition to a Heartland concordat.
